.TH "DCD.CONSOLE" "2" "27 October 2026" "" ""
.SH NAME
dcd.console \- DConnectDaemon - administration console
.SH SYNOPSIS

\fBtelnet\fR [ \fBhost name\fR ] [ \fBport number\fR ]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
This file describes, how to use administration console of DConnectDaemon.
.SH "LOGGING IN"
.PP
You can connect to cosole using \fBtelnet\fR command. The default port number is \fB511\fR. 
The file \fIconsole.allow\fR (default location \fI/usr/local/etc/dcd/\fR) contains list of hosts allowed to access the console.
After a connect you must enter login and password. Logins and passwords are stored in file \fIdcd.users\fR;
the password may be plaintext or a salted SHA-512 hash generated by \fBdcd.adduser\fR.
Accounts with the \fBc\fR permission can access the console. The same console is also
available in a browser at \fIhttp://host:PORT/console\fR when \fBlisten_port_http\fR is
enabled in \fIdcd.conf\fR (it bridges to the console port).
.SH "CONSOLE COMMANDS"
.PP
You can control the hub from console. The following commands are available:
.TP
\fBconf\fR
Show current configuration.
.TP
\fBrehash\fR
Reload configuration, ex. after config change. This command allows configuration change without server restart.
.TP
\fBquit\fR
Leave the console
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show the command list (grouped by categories).
.TP
\fBstat\fR
Show hub statistics: number of users, amount of shared data, hub's uptime, etc.
.TP
\fBstats [\fIreset\fB]\fR
Show runtime telemetry: traffic (TCP/UDP), per-command dispatch counts, user rotation (online, max online, logins/hour). With \fIreset\fR zero the counters.
.TP
\fBusers\fR
Show all hub users.
.TP
\fBshowops\fR
Show all hub operators.
.TP
\fBwho\fR
Show who is on the console. The command displays host address, idle time, etc.
.TP
\fBwhois <nick>\fR
Show user description.
.TP
\fBwhoip <ip>\fR
Show nicks using the specified IP.
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Show the hub version.
.TP
\fBuptime\fR
Show hub uptime.
.TP
\fBdate\fR [\fBtime\fR]
Show hub date and time.
.TP
\fBkick <nick> [\fIreason\fB]\fR
Disconnect a user \fI<nick>\fR from hub. Optional \fIreason\fR will be displayed on user's public chat window.
.TP
\fBpunish <nick> <type> [\fIminutes\fB] [\fIreason\fB]\fR
Punish a user (\fItype\fR: ban, nodl, nochat, nopblchat, noprvchat, nosearch).
.TP
\fBlspunished\fR
List punished users.
.TP
\fBamnesty <nick>\fR / \fBamnesty_all\fR
Remove penalty from a user / from all users.
.TP
\fBredirect <nick> <address>\fR / \fBredirect_all <address>\fR
Move a user (or all users) to another hub.
.TP
\fBmsg / msg_all / msg_prv / msg_prv_all / mmsg / mmsg_all\fR
Send message to a user / all users / as private / etc.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
